TI  - Dual-mode immunoassay for sensitive detection of ochratoxin a based on PP(Fe)@HRP 
      probe with high catalytic activity.
PG  - 150526
LID - S0308-8146(26)02686-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.foodchem.2026.150526 [doi]
AB  - Ochratoxin A (OTA) is a mycotoxin with carcinogenic properties. Thus, it is 
      essential to establish a sensitive method for detecting OTA. In this work, a 
      colorimetric and fluorescence dual-mode OTA immunoassay was established based on 
      PP(Fe)@HRP probe. The PP(Fe)@HRP probe consists of PCN-224(Fe), PtNPs and HRP, 
      all of which possess peroxidase activity. When combined to form PP(Fe)@HRP, the 
      peroxidase activity increased significantly. Then, the new probe was used to 
      oxidize TMB to generate blue signal. Meanwhile, the TMB oxidation product (oxTMB) 
      effectively quenched the fluorescence of GSH-AuNCs to generate fluorescence 
      signal. By modifying antibody onto this probe, linking them to the target OTA, an 
      ultra-sensitive dual-mode OTA immunoassay was achieved. This immunoassay 
      demonstrated excellent sensitivity. The limit of detection (LOD) of colorimetric 
      mode was 0.09 ng/mL, and the LOD of fluorescence mode was 0.02 ng/mL. Besides, 
      the immunoassay had high specificity toward OTA and satisfactory recovery rate in 
      corn samples.
