PMID- 42478663
OWN - NLM
STAT- Publisher
LR  - 20260721
IS  - 1759-9679 (Electronic)
IS  - 1759-9660 (Linking)
DP  - 2026 Jul 21
TI  - A washing-/enzyme-free chemiluminescent immunoassay for rapid and sensitive 
      on-site detection of prostate specific antigen.
LID - 10.1039/d6ay00542j [doi]
AB  - The abnormal expression of biomarkers is often closely related to the occurrence 
      and development of diseases. Quantification of biomarkers is critical for disease 
      diagnosis, treatment guidance, and prognosis evaluation. Herein, we presented a 
      washing-/enzyme-free chemiluminescent immunoassay (CLIA) for rapid and sensitive 
      on-site detection of prostate specific antigen (PSA). The gold magnetic 
      nanoparticles (Au@MNPs) modified with capture antibody (Ab(1)) ensured specific 
      capturing and effective enrichment of PSA in biological matrices via magnetic 
      separation. Meanwhile, the peroxidase-like activity of Au@MNPs enabled the 
      generation of chemiluminescence signals. The entire protocol is 
      washing-/enzyme-free, thus simplifying the analysis process, reducing 
      accumulative errors and overcoming the high cost and instability of natural 
      enzymes. The analytical performance was evaluated to be satisfactory by using a 
      highly integrated detection platform, and the limit of detection (LOD) was as low 
      as 0.41 pg mL(-1). Therefore, this approach proposed a rapid and sensitive 
      on-site detection method for biomarkers, which is of great significance for 
      disease screening in resource-poor settings.
