JID - 101763536
PMC - PMC13331620
OAB - Testing for parvovirus (B19V) and hepatitis A virus (HAV) is an important safety 
      step undertaken by commercial fractionators and some blood operators prior to 
      donor plasma fractionation. As part of a quality improvement process for 
      fractionated plasma, Canadian Blood Services assessed the operational potential 
      to undertake in-house testing for B19V and HAV nucleic acid testing (NAT). 
      Established thresholds for B19V were provided to Canadian Blood Services by 
      partnering fractionators, and no required threshold has been established for HAV. 
      An evaluation was completed by Canadian Blood Services using samples provided by 
      commercial sources to determine operational pool size for testing EDTA plasma 
      specimens for B19V and HAV NAT (Roche cobas DPX assay; Roche Diagnostics) using 
      the cobas Synergy System (consisting of the Hamilton Microlab STAR IVD Pipettor 
      and the cobas 6800 Test System).
