TI  - Broad-spectrum antibody based colorimetric immunoassay for highly sensitive 
      on-site quantitative detection of thirteen fluoroquinolones residues in aquatic 
      products.
PG  - 149713
LID - S0308-8146(26)01871-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.foodchem.2026.149713 [doi]
AB  - Highly sensitive on-site rapid detection of multiple fluoroquinolones (FQs) 
      residues in aquatic products is essential for ensuring food safety and regulating 
      antibiotic use. In this work, the broad-spectrum antibody and portable reader 
      based highly sensitive colorimetric immunoassay was developed for detection of 
      thirteen FQs residues in aquatic products. The developed colorimetric immunoassay 
      enables simultaneous semi-qualitative visual screening and quantitative detection 
      of thirteen FQs in 10 mins. The colorimetric immunoassay exhibits a visual 
      semi-qualitative limit of detection (LOD) of 2.0-4.0 mug/L by naked-eye. The 
      colorimetric immunoassay exhibits outstanding linearity across the concentration 
      range of 1.0-50.0 mug/L with an exceptionally low LOD of 0.83 mug/L. Application of 
      the colorimetric immunoassay in shrimps, tilapias and bullfrogs was successfully 
      carried out by HPLC and ELISA. This sensitive, accurate and rapid colorimetric 
      immunoassay can be applied to the detection of FQs in aquatic products in 
      multiple scenarios.
