TI  - Smartphone-integrated cascade immunosensing platform based on 
      antibody-enzyme-inorganic hybrid nanoflowers for highly sensitive detection of 
      zearalenone.
PG  - 119309
LID - S0963-9969(26)00986-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.foodres.2026.119309 [doi]
AB  - Zearalenone (ZEN), a toxic non-steroidal mycotoxin with strong bioaccumulation 
      potential, poses severe threats to food and public health, while conventional 
      detection methods suffer from poor stability, exogenous reagent dependence, or 
      limited on-site applicability. Herein, we report a cascade catalysis-driven, 
      smartphone-integrated immunosensing platform based on antibody-enzyme-inorganic 
      hybrid nanoflower (IgG-GOx-Pt@NiO/CoO HNFs) for highly sensitive and on-site 
      detection of ZEN. The unique hierarchical architecture of the hybrid nanoflower 
      dramatically boosts enzymatic activity and long-term stability, enabling 
      efficient signal amplification via glucose oxidase (GOx)-mediated oxidation of 
      glucose and subsequent H(2)O(2)-triggered colorimetric reaction of 
      3,3',5,5'-tetramethylbenzidine (TMB). Under optimal conditions, the colorimetric 
      immunoassay exhibits a broad linear range of 0.125-100 ng/mL and a low detection 
      limit (LOD) of 0.04 ng/mL. Furthermore, by integrating a smartphone app for 
      colorimetric readout, we constructed a portable sensing platform with a linear 
      range of 5-100 ng/mL and LOD of 1.67 ng/mL. This work highlights the synergistic 
      enhancement achieved through an integrated hybrid nanoflower architecture and the 
      smartphone-based mode enables instrument-free, on-site analysis with results 
      obtained in under 10 min. The results of 15 naturally contaminated real samples 
      showed good correlation between HPLC-MS/MS and the developed system. The proposed 
      strategy exhibited great potential for the rapid monitoring of mycotoxins or 
      other small molecule hazards.
