TI  - High-affinity monoclonal antibody pairs-based time-resolved fluorescent 
      microsphere-lateral flow and electrochemical immunosensing platforms for rapid 
      and quantitative detection of Helicobacter pylori in saliva.
PG  - 129920
LID - S0039-9140(26)00576-X [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.talanta.2026.129920 [doi]
AB  - Current diagnostic methods for Helicobacter pylori (H. pylori) infection suffer 
      from critical limitations. Endoscopy is invasive, while stool antigen tests and 
      urea breath tests require specialized laboratories and complex sample processing. 
      To address these unmet needs, we present a novel saliva-based point-of-care 
      platform for rapid and quantitative H. pylori detection. The platform consists of 
      two innovative biosensors: a time-resolved fluorescent microsphere-lateral flow 
      immunoassay strip (TRFM-LFIA) and an electrochemical immunosensor, specifically 
      designed for UreB antigen detection in unprocessed saliva. A high-affinity 
      monoclonal antibody pair (2-C2-F5/8-B5-E6) targeting non-overlapping UreB 
      epitopes was developed through integrated recombinant antigen expression, 
      hybridoma technology, and molecular docking. This antibody pair was applied to 
      both biosensors using a double-antibody sandwich format, achieving high 
      sensitivity (LOD: 91 pg/mL for TRFM-LFIA; 38.3 pg/mL for electrochemical 
      immunosensor) and broad dynamic range (0.1-1000 ng/mL) without sample 
      pre-treatment. Both biosensors demonstrated good specificity against common 
      interferents, with reproducibility below 8% coefficient of variation, and 100% 
      concordance with gold-standard diagnostics in 21 saliva samples (11 H. 
      pylori-positive, 10 healthy controls). Crucially, this work enables direct saliva 
      analysis, eliminating the need for invasive procedures and complex 
      infrastructure, thereby offering a scalable and cost-effective solution for 
      resource-limited settings.
