TI  - Establishment of an immunoassay for detection of melatonin and 2-mydroxymelatonin 
      based on computer-aided design.
PG  - 149476
LID - S0308-8146(26)01634-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.foodchem.2026.149476 [doi]
AB  - Melatonin (MT) is a popular ingredient in food and supplements due to its health 
      benefits. However, unregulated use and labeling inaccuracies in commercial 
      products pose safety risks. Establishing reliable monitoring methods is therefore 
      essential for consumer protection. In this study, haptens were screened through 
      computer simulations based on structural, charge, and electrostatic potential 
      properties. Using the selected optimal hapten, a monoclonal antibody capable of 
      simultaneously recognizing MT and 2-hydroxymelatonin (2-MT) was successfully 
      developed. The half-maximal inhibitory concentrations for MT and 2-MT were 
      47.89 ng/mL and 185.09 ng/mL, respectively. Furthermore, a colloidal gold 
      immunochromatographic assay was established to detect MT and 2-MT in milk, wine, 
      and tablets. The visual limit of detection was 20-100 ng/mL for MT and 
      50-200 ng/mL (or mug/kg) for 2-MT, respectively. The method demonstrated reliable 
      results when validated by LC-MS/MS. Meanwhile, the developed strips exhibited 
      good stability.
