TI  - Smartphone-integrated time-resolved fluorescent lateral flow immunoassay for 
      sensitive and on-site detection of thiamphenicol and florfenicol.
PG  - 129544
LID - S0039-9140(26)00199-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.talanta.2026.129544 [doi]
AB  - Thiamphenicol (TAP) and florfenicol (FF) residues in animal-derived foods pose 
      considerable human health concerns. Therefore, developing a rapid and sensitive 
      method for TAP and FF is necessary. In this study, a time-resolved fluorescent 
      microsphere-based lateral flow immunoassay (TRFM-LFIA) integrated with a 
      smartphone-based portable fluorescence analyzer was established for the rapid and 
      sensitive detection of TAP and FF in foods. Under optimal conditions, the limit 
      of detection of the TRFM-LFIA for TAP and FF was 0.02 ng/mL, which was 29.5- and 
      19.5-fold more sensitive than that of the conventional gold nanoparticles-based 
      lateral flow immunoassay. The recoveries of TAP and FF in spiked real samples 
      were 82.72%-114.10% and 103.78%-116.50%, respectively, with a coefficient of 
      variation of less than 13%. These results indicate that the smartphone-integrated 
      TRFM-LFIA can be used as an effective tool for the on-site detection of TAP and 
      FF in animal-derived foods.
